      {
        "id": 264720,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-12-29T17:34:38.350Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Christopher is wrong here, a countable infinity times another countable infinity is not an uncountable infinity.  It is simply a much, much larger countable infinity.  The amount of time needed to count it is also countably infinite, and both of these remain smaller than a truly uncountable infinity, such as the number of times units within literally forever.</p>\n<p>I honestly think the two Wagers Master might just play games with each other forever and leave everyone else alone.  Maybe that’s just me being an introverted only child who always wanted another me so I wouldn’t be alone; I’m giving them a happy ending, even though I hate them.</p>\n<p>Weird that the two Pre-OblivAeon “multiverse refugees” are both female, as is the most famous OA one, so the name “Mister” is definitely not even remotely possible to entertain for a moment.  I think the most notable male one is Hedgelord.</p>\n<p>The blank letter was kind of a good joke, but if I was writing a comic with Progeny in it, I’d give him a few word bubbles, containing things like “cannot destroy, must adapt with new element and then attempt to destroy again”, but better than that, very alien and robotic sounding and monstrous, but definitely not mindless.  It’s not that he can’t talk, just that he has no reason to engage in dialogue with things he intends to destroy.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-12-29T17:48:20.177Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
