      {
        "id": 264724,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-12-30T04:28:41.773Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Then clearly that is a flawed definition, as it stands to reason that if “size” of infinity can possibly mean anything, then the set of infinite numbers ending in 4 or 8 has to be twice as large as the number of infinite numbers ending in 8 only.  Any claim to the contrary defies basic logic in such a way that it cannot possibly be worth anything as scholarship.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-12-30T04:28:41.773Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": 26,
