        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-12-30T18:40:23.740Z",
        "cooked": "<p>And if it’s so “counterintuitive” as to require ignoring any real world applications as well as basic logic, then what exactly is the point of it?  It might as well not exist, if it’s only function is to amuse math nerds while confounding everyone else.  No such thing as actual infinity can exist in real space, the closest thing to an application I can think of is fractal drawings, which are best, sure, but I’m not certain that it’s necessary to have highly confusing math theorems to explain them, when other theorems more firmly grounded in reality might also do so.</p>",
